Z||000000||Shunyata||01-20-2001||03:42 AM||||'lo.<BR>am i the only one that finds it more or less impossible to check the oil on a v6? or at least, on mine? the dipstick always comes up either coated half way up the thing, or spotted up it so i cant tell what the level actually is. regardless of whether i check it cold, hot, warm... been this way since i bought it a few months ago. i know its not low 'cause i just changed the oil a month ago, but, i'd like to be able to check it in the future?<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Shun<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-20-2001||06:36 AM||||ya it is a problem. Dont know why they put in on the back. I usually pull it out once, wipe, and do it again to check it. a second time if I really want to be sure. before i switched to synthetic oil, it used to drop about 15 pounds oil pressure when it was a quart low too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shunyata||01-20-2001||07:04 AM||||i usually try putting it in/wiping it off taking it back out 2 or 3 times, and everytime i cant read the level, oil is just spotted up and down it.<P><P>------------------<BR>-Shun<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||01-20-2001||08:06 AM||||I've never had that problem. The oil isn't foaming or anything is it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||01-20-2001||08:39 AM||||I can't let this one slide by-- Shut the engine off first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodney||01-20-2001||10:50 AM||||I can answer why the dip stick is in the front of the engine but I'll see if anyone else can answer that. Easy trivia question.<P>To check the oil pull the dip stick out and clean it with a rag. Reinsert it but not all the way. That way it will not go into the oil in the pan. Take it out and clean it. Do that a few times then check you oil. That removes most of the oil from the tube. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||01-20-2001||11:21 AM||||ITs on the front, because in FWD applications it is easy to reach.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ka4nkf||01-20-2001||03:00 PM||||I agree with Shunyata. this has been a problem for me also. I change oil every 1000 miles and the oil is always so clean plus all the oil bubbles on the stick I just cant read where it is on stick. I been thinking  maybe if you could paint it some color so you can see it better. also maybe you could put a brush (like you clean the bore in a rifle)on a rod and clean the tube out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||01-20-2001||04:12 PM||||I knew that one Rodney but seems it would have been pretty simple to plug it and bore one on the back side.||||reg||1
Z||000009||2birds||01-20-2001||10:28 PM||||I just check mine when it's cold and all the oil has drained back out of the tube.  Worked fine for 13 years.||||reg||1
